_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 32
---
order: 32
---
short_label: III.32
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If a straight line touches a circle, and from the point of contact there is drawn across, in the circle, a straight line cutting the circle, then the angles which it makes with the tangent equal the angles in the alternate segments of the circle.
----
proof:

For let a straight line {EF} touch the circle {ABCD} at the point {B}, and from the point {B} let there be drawn across, in the circle {ABCD}, a straight line {BD} cutting it.

I say that the angles which {BD} makes with the tangent {EF} equal the angles in the alternate segments of the circle, that is, that the angle {FBD} equals the angle constructed in the segment {BAD|segBAD}, and the angle {EBD} equals the angle constructed in the segment {DCB|segDCB}.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="270" height="260" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="III.32 diagram" src="propIII32.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // The tangent-chord angle. Joyce's figure is the circle, the tangent EF,
    // the chord BD and the three joins; the proof names two SEGMENTS of the
    // circle (BAD, DCB), seven angles, the quadrilateral ABCD and the
    // triangle ABD, none of which the figure draws as elements. Everything
    // added here is fully transparent (;0;0;0 lines, ;0;0;0;0 circles /
    // sectors / polygons), so the resting figure is pixel-unchanged; the
    // names exist so a slide or a hover can light them.
    //
    // The circle is declared ABC but the proof calls it ABCD throughout, so
    // ABCD is a transparent twin: the real circle carries a random face and
    // a highlighted face is promoted within its pass (#140), which would
    // paint it over the angle markers. ABC is never named in a slide set.
    //
    // A segment is chord + arc. The chord BD is its own line; the arc is a
    // zero-colour sector, whose drawEdge strokes only the arc (no radii), so
    // the pair lights as the segment. Arm order decides WHICH arc a sector
    // draws (euclid#172), so both were checked against the bundle by pixel:
    // segBAD's arc passes A, segDCB's passes C. Neither is swept.
    //
    // Colour: equal angles share a colour — FBD = BAD orange, EBD = BCD
    // green; right angles red; ABD, the angle subtracted, keeps the palette
    // default. Same-vertex markers at B ring-step automatically (#103).
    var GIVEN = ["ABC","ABCD","O","B","D","BD","E","F","EF"];
    var SAY   = GIVEN.concat(["angFBD","angEBD","segBAD","segDCB"]);
    // Statement slides: the figure built in the statement's own order.
    var ST1 = ["ABC","ABCD","O","B","E","F","EF"];
    var ST2 = ST1.concat(["D","BD"]);
    var ST3 = ST2.concat(["angFBD","angEBD"]);
    var ST4 = ST3.concat(["segBAD","segDCB","P","PB","PD","angBPD","C","BC","CD","angBCD"]);
    var PERP  = SAY.concat(["A","AB"]);
    var JOINS = PERP.concat(["C","AD","CD","BC"]);
    var SEMI  = JOINS.concat(["angADB"]);
    var TRI   = SEMI.concat(["triABD","angBAD","angABD"]);
    var RT    = TRI.concat(["angABF"]);
    var QUAD  = RT.concat(["quadABCD","angBCD"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "III.32",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;130,30",
            "B;point;free;130,230",
            "AB;line;connect;A,B",
            "O;point;midpoint;AB;0;0",
            "ABC;circle;radius;O,B;0;0;black;random",
            "C;point;circleSlider;ABC,200,120",
            "D;point;circleSlider;ABC,160,80",
            "AD;line;connect;A,D",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D",
            "BE';line;perpendicular;B,A;0;0;0",
            "E;point;lineSlider;BE',30,230",
            "F;point;lineSlider;BE',230,230",
            "EF;line;connect;E,F",
            // Transparent twin of the circle, under the proof's name.
            "ABCD;circle;radius;O,B;0;0;0;0",
            // The two segments' arcs: B through A to D, and D through C to B.
            "segBAD;sector;sector;O,D,B;0;0;0;0",
            "segDCB;sector;sector;O,B,D;0;0;0;0",
            // The triangle the I.32 step is about, and the quadrilateral in
            // the circle for III.22. Explicit ;0 faces — an omitted faceColor
            // is an opaque near-white face.
            "triABD;polygon;triangle;A,B,D;0;0;0;0",
            "quadABCD;polygon;quadrilateral;A,B,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            // Angle markers, hidden in the resting figure (showAngles
            // defaults false). Equal angles share a colour.
            "angFBD;sector;angleMarker;B,F,D;0;0;orange;orange",
            "angEBD;sector;angleMarker;B,E,D;0;0;mediumseagreen;mediumseagreen",
            "angADB;sector;angleMarkerRight;D,A,B;0;0;red;red",
            "angBAD;sector;angleMarker;A,B,D;0;0;orange;orange",
            "angABD;sector;angleMarker;B,A,D",
            "angABF;sector;angleMarkerRight;B,A,F;0;0;red;red",
            "angBCD;sector;angleMarker;C,B,D;0;0;mediumseagreen;mediumseagreen",
            // For the statement slides only: an unlettered point P in the
            // segment BAD, joined to B and D, so "the angle in the alternate
            // segment" can be shown — and swung along its arc to show it
            // stays equal to FBD wherever it is. Hidden at rest.
            "P;point;circleSlider;ABC,60,130;0",
            "PB;line;connect;P,B",
            "PD;line;connect;P,D",
            "angBPD;sector;angleMarker;P,B,D;0;0;orange;orange"
        ],
        // Draggables are auto-unioned into every slide. Dumping `draggable`
        // against the bundle gives A, B, C, D, E, F. The proof draws BA and
        // takes C at random only after the "I say" — so A and C are deferred
        // and follow `visible`; B, D, E, F are the givens of slide 1. The
        // resting figure is unaffected.
        deferDraggables: ["A","C","P"],
        initiallyHidden: ["P","PB","PD","angBPD"],
        aliases: { "BA": "AB", "DC": "CD", "CB": "BC",
                   "FBD": "angFBD", "DBF": "angFBD",
                   "EBD": "angEBD", "DBE": "angEBD",
                   "ADB": "angADB", "BAD": "angBAD", "ABD": "angABD",
                   "ABF": "angABF", "BCD": "angBCD", "DCB": "angBCD" },
        slides: [
            // The deck opens on the proposition's statement over the givens
            // (process.md “Open on the statement”), split at its seams.
            { text: "“If {a straight line|EF} touches {a circle|ABCD},”",
              visible: ST1,
              highlighted: ["EF","B"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "EF", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "“and from {the point of contact|B} there is drawn across, in the circle, {a straight line cutting the circle|BD},”",
              visible: ST2,
              highlighted: ["BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "“then the angles which it makes with {the tangent|EF}”",
              visible: ST3,
              highlighted: ["angFBD","angEBD","EF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "angFBD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angEBD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            // Each angle in an alternate segment shares its tangent angle's
            // colour; P and C then travel their arcs and back, and the
            // markers stay matched — "equal" shown as invariance.
            { text: "“equal the angles in the alternate segments of the circle.”",
              visible: ST4,
              highlighted: ["angFBD","angBPD","angEBD","angBCD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "PB", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "PD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angBPD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "BC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "CD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "angBCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "P", name: geomlib.A.Point.followPath, args: { arc: { center: "O", sweep: 55 } } },
                  { elem: "C", name: geomlib.A.Point.followPath, args: { arc: { center: "O", sweep: -30 } } } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "III.32" }] },
            { text: "For let a straight line {EF} touch the circle {ABCD} at the point {B}, and from the point {B} let there be drawn across, in the circle {ABCD}, a straight line {BD} cutting it.",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["EF", "B", "BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] } },
            { text: "I say that the angles which {BD} makes with the tangent {EF} equal the angles in the alternate segments of the circle,",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["BD","EF"] },
            { text: "that is, that the angle {FBD} equals the angle constructed in the segment {BAD|segBAD}, and the angle {EBD} equals the angle constructed in the segment {DCB|segDCB}.",
              visible: SAY,
              // The two markers are the animation's targets; the segments
              // they are compared with carry the gold.
              highlighted: ["segBAD","segDCB","BD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angFBD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angEBD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Draw {BA} from {B} at right angles to {EF},",
              visible: PERP,
              highlighted: ["EF"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AB", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "A",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "BA at right angles to EF", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "take a point {C} at random on the circumference {BD|segDCB}, and join {AD}, {DC}, and {CB}.",
              visible: JOINS,
              highlighted: ["segDCB"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "C",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "AD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "CD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Then, since a straight line {EF} touches the circle {ABCD} at {B}, and {BA} has been drawn from the point of contact at right angles to the tangent, the center of the circle {ABCD} is on {BA}.",
              visible: JOINS,
              // O is Joyce's own colourless centre point; highlighted, it
              // shows as a bare gold dot on BA — no letter, since its
              // nameColor is 0.
              highlighted: ["EF","AB","ABCD","O"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "the center lies on the perpendicular from the point of contact", ref: "III.19" }] },
            { text: "Therefore {BA} is a diameter of the circle {ABCD}.",
              visible: JOINS,
              highlighted: ["AB","O","ABCD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "a chord through the center", ref: "I.Def.17" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the angle {ADB}, being an angle in a semicircle, is right.",
              visible: SEMI,
              highlighted: ["segBAD","BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angADB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the angle in a semicircle is right", ref: "III.31" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the sum of the remaining angles {BAD} and {ABD} equals one right angle.",
              visible: TRI,
              highlighted: ["triABD","angADB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBAD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angABD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "the three angles of the triangle ABD equal two right angles", ref: "I.32" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {ABF} is also right, therefore the angle {ABF} equals the sum of the angles {BAD} and {ABD}.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["angBAD","angABD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angABF", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "ABF is right, BA being at right angles to EF", ref: "I.11" }] },
            { text: "Subtract the angle {ABD} from each.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["angABD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "C.N.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the remaining angle {DBF} equals the angle {BAD} in the alternate segment of the circle.",
              visible: RT,
              highlighted: ["angFBD","angBAD","segBAD"] },
            { text: "Next, since {ABCD|quadABCD} is a quadrilateral in a circle, the sum of its opposite angles equals two right angles.",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["angBAD"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "quadABCD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "angBCD",   name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "opposite angles of a quadrilateral in a circle", ref: "III.22" }] },
            { text: "But the sum of the angles {DBF} and {DBE} also equals two right angles, therefore the sum of the angles {DBF} and {DBE} equals the sum of the angles {BAD} and {BCD},",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["angFBD","angEBD","angBAD","angBCD"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "DBF and DBE stand on the straight line EF", ref: "I.13" }] },
            { text: "of which the angle {BAD} was proved equal to the angle {DBF},",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["angBAD","angFBD"] },
            { text: "therefore the remaining angle {DBE} equals the angle {DCB} in the alternate segment {DCB|segDCB} of the circle.",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["angEBD","angBCD","segDCB"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "C.N.3" }] },
            { text: "Therefore if a straight line touches a circle, and from the point of contact there is drawn across, in the circle, a straight line cutting the circle, then the angles which it makes with the tangent equal the angles in the alternate segments of the circle.",
              visible: QUAD,
              highlighted: ["EF","BD","angFBD","angBAD","angEBD","angBCD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "III.32") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Def.17": "/elements/books/bookI/definitions/defI17/",
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "I.11":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI11/",
        "I.13":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI13/",
        "I.32":     "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI32/",
        "III.19":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII19/",
        "III.22":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII22/",
        "III.31":   "/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII31/",
        "C.N.3":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn3/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Draw {BA} from {B} at right angles to {EF}, take a point {C} at random on the circumference {BD|segDCB}, and join {AD}, {DC}, and {CB}. [!just I.11]

Then, since a straight line {EF} touches the circle {ABCD} at {B}, and {BA} has been drawn from the point of contact at right angles to the tangent, the center of the circle {ABCD} is on {BA}. [!just III.19]

Therefore {BA} is a diameter of the circle {ABCD}.  Therefore the angle {ADB}, being an angle in a semicircle, is right. [!just III.31]

Therefore the sum of the remaining angles {BAD} and {ABD} equals one right angle. [!just I.32]

But the angle {ABF} is also right, therefore the angle {ABF} equals the sum of the angles {BAD} and {ABD}.

Subtract the angle {ABD} from each.  Therefore the remaining angle {DBF} equals the angle {BAD} in the alternate segment of the circle.

Next, since {ABCD|quadABCD} is a quadrilateral in a circle, the sum of its opposite angles equals two right angles. [!just III.22]

But the sum of the angles {DBF} and {DBE} also equals two right angles, therefore the sum of the angles {DBF} and {DBE} equals the sum of the angles {BAD} and {BCD}, of which the angle {BAD} was proved equal to the angle {DBF}, therefore the remaining angle {DBE} equals the angle {DCB} in the alternate segment {DCB|segDCB} of the circle.

Therefore *if a straight line touches a circle, and from the point of contact there is drawn across, in the circle, a straight line cutting the circle, then the angles which it makes with the tangent equal the angles in the alternate segments of the circle.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide: This proposition is used in the next two propositions and a couple of the propositions in Book IV.
